#. Translators: What's new for this version, shown in the add-on store.
#. Markdown: NVDA renders it and reads it line by line.
#: manifest.ini:changelog
msgid ""
"- New: the heating of a Netatmo thermostat is recorded in the history, every switching as an event and as a series with the share of time it was active.\n"
"- NVDA no longer crashes when the device menu is closed after a device was switched from the favourites tab.\n"
"- Enter or Space on a VeSync or Cozytouch device no longer freezes NVDA.\n"
"- Meross leak sensors are read correctly, and several sensors on one hub each keep their own values.\n"
"- Meross messages are counted as the cloud counts them, so a device stays below its hourly limit with the device menu open.\n"
"- Meross garage door openers and roller shutters are shown but not switched.\n"
"- The Netatmo device menu offers \"Add to favorites\" again, and the relay shows its heating state, Wi-Fi and radio signal.\n"
"- A Cozytouch command the appliance takes over late is announced as sent and confirmed once it arrives.\n"
"- The history no longer records a change made here a second time as made elsewhere, and it records maintenance falling due, a low battery and the end of an air fryer programme.\n"
"- A temperature set in the Netatmo app is one history entry with its end time; an open window is recorded too.\n"
"- A Meross account with two-factor authentication is named as the reason the sign-in fails, and a Cozytouch server fault at sign-in is retried.\n"
"- The settings of the add-on are stored in the base configuration, not in the active profile. With \"Save configuration when exiting NVDA\" switched off, they are saved with NVDA+Ctrl+C like all other settings.\n"
"- The CSV export of the history uses the separators of the Windows region.\n"
"- NVDA exits faster on a slow network.\n"
"- Credentials are no longer sent along when a cloud redirects to another host, and a foreign call of the Netatmo callback address no longer ends the sign-in.\n"
"- Certificates are checked against the add-on's own, current root certificates, and the bundled aiohttp is updated to 3.14.5."
msgstr ""

